'''Stockbridge Common Marsh''' is a {{convert| 64.8 |ha|acre|abbr=off|adj=on}} biological [[Site of Special Scientific Interest]] south of [[Stockbridge, Hampshire|Stockbridge]] in [[Hampshire]].<ref name=dsv>{{cite web|url= https://designatedsites.naturalengland.org.uk/SiteDetail.aspx?SiteCode=S1000182&SiteName=&countyCode=19&responsiblePerson=&SeaArea=&IFCAArea=  |title=Designated Sites View: Stockbridge Common Marsh| series= Sites of Special Scientific Interest|publisher=Natural England|accessdate =19 May 2020}}</ref><ref name=map>{{cite web|url=https://magic.defra.gov.uk/MagicMap.aspx?startTopic=Designations&activelayer=sssiIndex&query=HYPERLINK%3D%271000182%27 |title=Map of Stockbridge Common Marsh|series= Sites of Special Scientific Interest|publisher=Natural England|accessdate=  19 May 2020}}</ref> It is owned by the [[National Trust]].<ref>{{cite web|url=  https://www.nationaltrust.org.uk/mottisfont/features/stockbridge-marsh |title=  Stockbridge Marsh |publisher=National Trust| accessdate= 19 May 2020}}</ref>

This site stretches for {{convert|2|km|mi|abbr=off}} along the flood plain of the [[River Test]]. It has wetland habitats including marsh, fen, [[Carr (landform)|carr]], [[alluvial]] meadows and a large shallow lake. The marsh has a rich variety of flora, with 180 species of flowering plants, including [[bog pimpernel]], [[Ophioglossum  vulgatum|adder’s-tongue fern]], [[Valeriana dioica| marsh  valerian]] and [[Menyanthes  trifoliata|bogbean]].<ref>{{cite web|url= https://designatedsites.naturalengland.org.uk/PDFsForWeb/Citation/1000182.pdf  |title=Stockbridge Common Marsh citation|series= Sites of Special Scientific Interest|publisher=Natural England|accessdate=   19 May 2020}}</ref>

