'''Stockbridge Down''' is a {{convert| 69.8 |ha|acre|abbr=off|adj=on}} biological [[Site of Special Scientific Interest]] east of [[Stockbridge, Hampshire|Stockbridge]] in [[Hampshire]].<ref name=dsv>{{cite web|url=  https://designatedsites.naturalengland.org.uk/SiteDetail.aspx?SiteCode=S1003407&SiteName=&countyCode=19&responsiblePerson=&SeaArea=&IFCAArea= |title=Designated Sites View: Stockbridge Down | series= Sites of Special Scientific Interest|publisher=Natural England|accessdate = 19 May 2020}}</ref><ref name=map>{{cite web|url=https://magic.defra.gov.uk/MagicMap.aspx?startTopic=Designations&activelayer=sssiIndex&query=HYPERLINK%3D%271003407%27 |title=Map of Stockbridge Down|series= Sites of Special Scientific Interest|publisher=Natural England|accessdate= 19 May 2020}}</ref> It is a [[Nature Conservation Review]] site, Grade 2.<ref>{{cite book|editor-first=Derek |editor-last=Ratcliffe  |title=A Nature Conservation Review|volume=2 |page= 130|authorlink=Derek Ratcliffe |publisher= Cambridge University Press|location =Cambridge, UK  |year=1977|isbn= 0521-21403-3 }}</ref> It is owned by the [[National Trust for Places of Historic Interest or Natural Beauty|National Trust]] and parts of it are designated as [[scheduled monument]]s, including an [[Iron Age]] hillfort ([[Woolbury]]) and fourteen [[Bronze Age]] burial mounds.<ref>{{cite web|url=  https://www.nationaltrust.org.uk/mottisfont/features/stockbridge-down |title= Stockbridge Down  |publisher=National Trust| accessdate= 24 April 2020}}</ref><ref>{{NHLE |num=1003531  |desc=Woolbury Ring, Stockbridge |grade=scheduled|access-date=22 December 2024}}</ref>

This site has a variety of scrub and grassland habitats on a north-west facing slope of chalk and a [[clay-with-flints]] plateau. There is a diverse range of butterflies, such as [[chalk-hill blue]], [[Melanargia galathea|marbled white]] and [[dark green fritillary]], while moths include the [[oblique striped]].<ref>{{cite web|url=  https://designatedsites.naturalengland.org.uk/PDFsForWeb/Citation/1003407.pdf |title=Stockbridge Down |type=SSSI citation|series= Sites of Special Scientific Interest|publisher=Natural England|accessdate=19 May 2020}}</ref>

